white-space: nowrap collapses runs of white space exactly like normal; it
only stops wrapping. Per CSS Text 3 (https://www.w3.org/TR/css-text-3/#white-space-property),
only pre, pre-wrap and break-spaces preserve spaces and pre-line preserves
line breaks, so a define body called under nowrap is re-indented. The
two-keyword form (collapse nowrap) means the same.
-- input.gohtml --
<style>main p { white-space: nowrap; } main li { white-space: collapse nowrap; }</style>
{{define "GET /x X()"}}{{template "p" .}}{{end}}
{{define "p"}}
<body>
<main>
<p>x</p>
<p>a
     b</p>
<ul>
<li>c
  d</li>
</ul>
</main>
</body>
{{end}}
-- format.gohtml --
<style>main p { white-space: nowrap; } main li { white-space: collapse nowrap; }</style>
{{define "GET /x X()"}}{{template "p" .}}{{end}}
{{define "p"}}
<body>
	<main>
		<p>x</p>
		<p>a
			b</p>
		<ul>
			<li>c
				d</li>
		</ul>
	</main>
</body>
{{end}}
